From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:10:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] signal: report an atomic store's permission fault as a write

The SIGBUS path labels a data fault's direction from the opcode: the
load/store classes with bit 22 clear are stores. An LSE atomic (LDADDAL,
SWPAL, which FEX emits for an x86 lock add or xchg) has bit 22 set as its
acquire bit, so its write-permission fault was raised as a read. FEX
services a write to a page it keeps read-only for self-modifying code,
not a read: an i386 Wine Mono, patching a call in code it had just
compiled with a lock-prefixed instruction, got an access violation
(read of 02793484 at eip 7a7d6b68) and hello32.exe ended c0000005.

Take a data abort's ISS.WnR as well, which the architecture sets for a
write, an atomic included; cache maintenance (ISS.CM) also sets it and
is left as it was.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-i386-dotnet.md
Offered-upstream: no; the iOS SIGBUS path is Madeira's own code
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 2a411d6..fc6fe5a 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -11982,6 +11982,17 @@ static void bus_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *sigcontext )
                 if ((f_insn & 0x0a000000) == 0x08000000 && !(f_insn & 0x00400000))
                     vrec.ExceptionInformation[0] = EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT;
             }
+            {
+                /* A data abort's ISS.WnR names the direction where the opcode test
+                 * cannot: an LSE atomic (LDADDAL, SWPAL: an x86 lock add or xchg
+                 * under FEX) has bit 22 set, yet faults as a write. FEX services a
+                 * write to a page it protects for self-modifying code; a read is
+                 * raised to the guest. Cache maintenance (ISS.CM) reports WnR=1 too. */
+                DWORD64 esr = get_fault_esr( bus_ctx );
+                unsigned ec = (unsigned)(esr >> 26);
+                if ((ec == 0x24 || ec == 0x25) && (esr & (1u << 6)) && !(esr & (1u << 8)))
+                    vrec.ExceptionInformation[0] = EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT;
+            }
 
             if (!virtual_handle_fault( get_thread_data(), &vrec, (void *)SP_sig(bus_ctx) ))
             {
